  ]
}
```

**Milestone Design Rationale Summary:**

| Aspect | Decision | Reasoning |
|--------|----------|-----------|
| **Rule type** | `inventory_has` | Preferred mapping for mine tasks — the mined item ends up in inventory |
| **Item ID** | `jungle_door` | Bare name (no `minecraft:` prefix) per evaluator convention |
| **min_count** | `1` | Only one door exists in the scene; player needs to collect it |
| **Why not `count_in_box_at_most`?** | Less robust | Would only confirm the block was removed, not that the player collected the drop |
| **Why not `mine_block` event?** | `inventory_has` preferred | Per design philosophy, inventory checks are the first-choice rule for mine tasks |
| **Why no position rule?** | Not a navigation task | The task is about mining, not reaching a location — position rules would over-specify |

The milestone is minimal (one rule), directly verifiable, and aligned with the design philosophy of preferring object-state rules over spatial constraints. The benchmark is ready for production.

